<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Public web measurement scanner</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Public web measurement scanner</h1>
      <p>
        This host identifies a bounded academic study of access to public websites. It performs
        domain characterization, not vulnerability scanning, authentication, or bulk collection.
      </p>

      <h2>Identification</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>User-Agent</dt>
        <dd><code>REPLACE_USER_AGENT</code></dd>
        <dt>Source addresses</dt>
        <dd><code>REPLACE_SOURCE_ADDRESSES</code></dd>
        <dt>Reverse DNS</dt>
        <dd><code>REPLACE_REVERSE_DNS</code></dd>
      </dl>

      <h2>Collection limits</h2>
      <p>
        Requests are rate-limited, bounded by per-domain request, response-byte, redirect, and
        wall-clock limits, and preceded by a robots.txt policy check. The scanner does not sign in,
        submit forms, bypass controls, or retain page text in its browser observations.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact and opt-out</h2>
      <p>
        For questions, corrections, complaints, or an opt-out request, contact
        <a href="REPLACE_CONTACT_URI">REPLACE_CONTACT_URI</a>. Include the affected domain and the
        requested scope. Do not send passwords, API keys, or other secrets.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
